# Graphify exclusions (gitignore syntax; .gitignore rules are merged automatically,
# so node_modules/, build output, etc. are already covered).
#
# Policy (HANDOFF.md, stage 2.4): graphs are structural knowledge over the
# modernized source. Docs belong to OpenWiki, not Graphify; historical source is
# never consumed raw (AGENTS.md); generated artifacts are noise.
#
# Per-module graphs are NOT configured here — run graphify separately per module
# (importer/, ir/, later engine/), each producing its own graphify-out/.

# Historical reference source — AGENTS.md forbids Graphify consuming raw ZIL/C++
original-projects/

# Documentation and prose (OpenWiki's domain, not structural)
*.md
wiki/
LICENSE
NOTICE

# Images and other non-code media
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.svg
*.ico
*.bmp

# Generated / committed artifacts (regenerable, high-noise)
importer/artifacts/
ir/artifacts/
package-lock.json

# Package/toolchain config — contributes ~30% of graph nodes as pure metadata
# noise (name/version/compilerOptions...), no structural signal
package.json
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.build.json

# Verification ground truth (transcripts, goldens, harness) — not engine source
verification/

# Graph outputs themselves — never self-ingest
graph/
graphify-out/

# Keep IR sample data eligible: the IR world (rooms/exits/objects) is itself a
# graph subject for stage 2.4 (no rule needed — .json is included by default;
# this note guards against adding a blanket *.json rule later)
